  "title": "AIDC: what-if chiller upgrade, CDU removal, upgrade over a dead primary",
  "description": "Counterfactual branch checks on the AIDC baseline: upgrading the single chiller group to N+1 (intact facility) must remove the chiller's SPOF finding from both chilled-water services and flip the chilled-water service's first-fault tolerance; removing the CDU must lose the cooling service exactly as its fault cascade does while the rack stays power-fed; and upgrading the same chiller group while the primary is already faulted must restore the lost services but abstain from the SPOF-path verdict — the counterfactual snapshot has one live group member, so the lone standby is itself a single point of failure and the verdict is stated as an abstention rather than asserted. Adjudicates Category 5 (what-if consistency, including the abstention path) for the AIDC segment.",
